lmcache: bind the Prometheus /metrics endpoint to 127.0.0.1 by default

What: a --prometheus-host flag (ObservabilityConfig.prometheus_host, default
  127.0.0.1) passed to prometheus_client.start_http_server(addr=...) in
  init_otel_metrics; the startup log prints the real address.
Why: with metrics on and no --otlp-endpoint, otel_init.py:117 called
  start_http_server(9090) with no address, so it listened on 0.0.0.0:9090 on
  every interface of c4130. Loopback by default; services.lmcache-sm70.
  metricsHost sets another address when a scraper needs it.
Upstream-files: lmcache/v1/mp_observability/{config,otel_init}.py (LMCache sdist)
Kill-switch: --prometheus-host 0.0.0.0 (upstream behaviour)

